        { q: "Outline why the student should use a small current and switch off between readings.", marks: 2, markscheme: ["A large current heats the wire ✓", "Resistance (resistivity) increases with temperature, so the readings would not be for a constant temperature ✓"] },
        { q: "Sketch the I–V characteristic of a filament lamp and explain its shape.", marks: 3, markscheme: ["Curve through the origin, symmetrical for negative V, with gradient decreasing as |V| increases ✓", "As current increases the filament temperature rises ✓", "Lattice ions vibrate more, so collisions increase and resistance rises (non-ohmic) ✓"] }
